Guest assets prepared for the OSS release (not published)
--------------------------------------------------------
Image.arm64: Alpine linux-virt 6.18.52-r0 (6.18.52-0-virt), GPL-2.0-only.
It is byte-identical to the decompressed kernel in the official Alpine 3.24.2
aarch64 netboot vmlinuz-virt. The exact Alpine build/patch/config sources are at
aports commit 09a165f4c951edf370eddde03b2d1d5fd71805ed, main/linux-lts.
Kernel syscall headers have the documented Linux-syscall-note; this does not
relicense the kernel binary under Apache-2.0.

rootfs.arm64.cpio.gz: Alpine minirootfs 3.24.2 aarch64 (83 base regular files
match the official archive), Aleph init/runner source and 190 signed offline
APKs. There are also 16 packages already installed in the base. All 190 APK RSA
signatures and payload hashes were verified with the Alpine signing key from
the checksum-verified official minirootfs. Each package retains its original
license, not the root Apache-2.0 license. The full package/version/license/origin
and pinned Alpine source-commit inventory is in deploy/guest/PACKAGES.tsv.

The payload includes GPL-2.0, GPL-3.0, LGPL-2.x/3.0, MPL, MIT/BSD, Apache-2.0,
Qt exceptions, font/data and other license expressions. Exact corresponding
sources, Alpine patches/config/build/install metadata and original notice texts
are in the separate release asset aleph-0.1.2-guest-sources.tar.zst.
All 206 package versions match their pinned recipes; all 509 packaging inputs
are checked by SHA-512. Kernel source/config/patch provenance is complete.
Pandoc's 257 locked Haskell dependencies and libglycin's 303 checksum-pinned
Rust crates are included, with original notices and recovered workspace licenses.

